WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.362
From April to June 2026,

2
00:00:02.462 --> 00:00:04.211
India imported 86 billion

3
00:00:04.211 --> 00:00:06.729
dollars more goods than it exported.

4
00:00:07.179 --> 00:00:09.354
Yet its current account deficit

5
00:00:09.354 --> 00:00:10.827
was just 4.2 billion:

6
00:00:10.977 --> 00:00:12.747
half a percent of GDP.

7
00:00:13.247 --> 00:00:14.642
Why? The current account

8
00:00:14.642 --> 00:00:16.037
also counts services and

9
00:00:16.037 --> 00:00:16.618
transfers.

10
00:00:16.918 --> 00:00:19.798
Net services brought in 51.6 billion;

11
00:00:19.918 --> 00:00:22.777
remittance receipts, 42.9 billion.

12
00:00:23.227 --> 00:00:25.147
The other side records investment:

13
00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:27.229
textbooks call it the capital account;

14
00:00:27.329 --> 00:00:30.145
RBI data calls it the financial account.

15
00:00:30.595 --> 00:00:32.899
That quarter, direct investment came in,

16
00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.919
while portfolio money flowed out.

17
00:00:35.369 --> 00:00:36.905
Goods tell half the story.

18
00:00:37.105 --> 00:00:38.709
Services and remittances

19
00:00:38.709 --> 00:00:39.644
tell the rest.

20
00:00:40.144 --> 00:00:41.040
Your turn.

21
00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:43.296
Which account records remittances

22
00:00:43.296 --> 00:00:44.007
from abroad?
